<section class="section section--surface" id="what-it-is-worth">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--phi">
      <p class="eyebrow">Worth knowing</p>
      <h2>Your last survey sets the clock on the next leak.</h2>
      <p>Subpart W counts a leak as open since the last survey, or all year if you surveyed once.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="ruled-left">
      <li><h3>Shorter assumed duration</h3><p>More documented surveys, shorter windows.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Consistent inventory inputs</h3><p>Closures write the fugitive emission record as the work happens.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Proof on the same record</h3><p>Repair, retest, and verification sit with the finding.</p></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note-ref">40 CFR 98.233(q), Equation W-30. Survey frequency and repair timelines come from NSPS OOOOB and state programs.</p>
  </div>
</section>

