<section class="section section--surface" id="us-regulations">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--phi">
      <p class="eyebrow">US regulations</p>
      <h2>One record for OOOOB/C and Subpart W.</h2>
      <p>OOOOB/C sets when you survey and repair. Subpart W turns findings into reported emissions. Both use the same component records.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="ruled-left">
      <li><h3>NSPS OOOOB/C fugitive programs</h3><p>Survey frequency, repair clocks, and Delay of Repair, tracked on the finding.</p></li>
      <li><h3>GHG Reporting Program Subpart W</h3><p>Leaks, survey dates, and open days feed the annual report.</p></li>
      <li><h3>State programs on top</h3><p>Stricter rules such as Colorado Regulation 7, configured per facility.</p></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="marker-note">Capture once, report from the same record: to the state, to EPA, and to the auditor.</p>
  </div>
</section>

